cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "drift" in publications use:'
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'drift: Detecting Riparian and Inland Floodplain Transitions'
version: 0.24.3
abstract: Fetch free global land-cover maps (Esri IO LULC, ESA WorldCover) or your
  own classified rasters for any area, such as a floodplain, compare them between
  two dates and across every year of a series, and turn the change into maps, tables
  and change polygons. Fetch dated Sentinel-2 composites and Esri Wayback imagery
  to check mapped change against, estimate accuracy and error-adjusted area from a
  stratified reference sample, and tag change areas with overlapping records such
  as fire perimeters or cutblocks. Under active development.
